          "value": "FIFO-empty timeout. Limits the APB access cycles an empty FIFO-data read may wait before returning PSLVERR.\n\nUsage: Program before DMA reads; zero gives an immediate error in the first access cycle when FIFO is empty; data available on the terminal decision cycle wins.\n\nValues:\n0x0 immediate empty-read timeout (reset value);\n0x1 to 0xFFFFFFFF wait the programmed number of APB access cycles.\n\nUnit: APB clock cycles\n\nLimits: 32-bit unsigned count; applies only while a FIFO-data read is active and the FIFO is empty.",
